    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: deterministic, `(lastName, postcode)`-keyed households\n\nThe household is now identified by a deterministic id derived from the last name and postcode, so members share it automatically \u2014 rather than a link created on demand by `sharesHousehold`.\n\n**`HouseholdIdGenerator`** (`service/HouseholdIdGenerator.java`)\n- `generate(lastName, postcode)` now returns the first 12 hex characters of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`. The `canonical(...)` normalizer (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case) is applied to the last name. Dropped the old address-based key and the `HH-`/upper-case formatting.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl`** (+ `ClinicService` interface)\n- `assignHousehold(owner)` now just derives and sets the deterministic id whenever the owner has a postcode (returns `null` for no postcode); no more member back-filling.\n- `existsOwnerInHousehold(owner)` and `countHouseholdMembers(owner)` are re-keyed onto the owner and its household. The private `findHouseholdMembers(owner)` matches existing owners by last name (case-insensitive) **and postcode** \u2014 the same key the id is built from \u2014 so the household-size that feeds membership is computed off the real household.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`**\n- Always assigns the deterministic `householdId` up front (so it's present on every owner and forms part of the identity key).\n- The household-duplicate block: a second owner in an existing household returns **409 CONFLICT** *unless* `sharesHousehold` is set, in which case it's created as a declared member. `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses this block \u2014 it no longer creates the link.\n- A declared household member is **not** run through the possible-duplicate flagging, so it's never marked a suspected duplicate. The exact identity-key duplicate check is preserved.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` descriptions/example to reflect the new `(lastName, postcode)` semantics.\n\nI verified the observable contract with temporary acceptance tests (same lastName+postcode \u2192 same id / 409 without `sharesHousehold` / created-and-not-flagged with it), then removed them. The existing `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite pass.\n\nOne note: `householdSize` is computed and persisted but isn't exposed on the `OwnerDto`, so it isn't observable via the API \u2014 I couldn't assert it end-to-end, only that it's now derived from the `(lastName, postcode)` household.",
